      <floats-group id="article-17974.s18">
        <fig id="article-17974.image.f2" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Electrocardiogram of Typical AVNRT With Pseudo-S Waves. This 12-lead electrocardiogram demonstrates typical (slow-fast) atrioventricular nodal reentrant tachycardia (top panel) featuring characteristic terminal pseudo-S waves, representing retrograde P-wave activity, which are absent in the baseline sinus rhythm (bottom panel). Contributed by I Ahmed, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Pseudo__s__waves" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
